{"id": "EUVD-2026-103645", "enisaUuid": "dbb58b84-b14a-3148-bd25-024c7dcd1025", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: RFCOMM: Reject short EA=0 frames in rfcomm_recv_frame()\n\nWhile rfcomm_recv_frame() verifies that skb->len is at least\nsizeof(*hdr) + 1 (4 bytes: 3-byte header + 1-byte FCS), an RFCOMM frame\nwith an extended 2-byte length field (!__test_ea(hdr->len)) has a 4-byte\nheader plus a 1-byte FCS (5 bytes minimum, sizeof(*hdr) + 2).\n\nWhen a 4-byte RFCOMM frame with EA == 0 arrives:\n1. The initial skb->len < sizeof(*hdr) + 1 check passes (4 < 4 is false).\n2. Trimming the FCS byte decrements skb->len to 3.\n3. If __check_fcs() succeeds, skb_pull(skb, 4) fails (4 > 3) and returns\n   NULL without advancing skb->data.\n4. Because the return value of skb_pull() is ignored, the un-pulled\n   3-byte struct rfcomm_hdr remains at skb->data and is either queued as\n   application payload via rfcomm_recv_data() or parsed as a multiplexer\n   control command via rfcomm_recv_mcc() on DLCI 0.\n\nFix this by extending the length check in rfcomm_recv_frame() to also\nrequire skb->len >= sizeof(*hdr) + 2 when !__test_ea(hdr->len).", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:19:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:22:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/76876fd26569302d26d91cbe8b75fa8e66cf8969", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97711b964877242933484989224a3c4c5d88a5ee", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7a1781a2f3a9667b3065d402d1f11986a2363e08", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c25587fa26761e623198b4f47151fe79d09ccde6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71ccacde407b7d8f0ef48974a0d2524602fd5c44", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/be00deee60044ffa820f9436415caeb665b2cda0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9240fc1f2cde5331c61608da21b00394602ca762", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d91041bb38b97e2feb625123cc0529d7b83a0e1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hpgr-cqmv-php2", "CVE-2026-98600"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1511822f-6e4e-344a-9309-0278eb8393f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.2"}, {"id": "1817b1ef-e1c4-3824-87b0-80810a09d350", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b230e5bf501c5edaf2eb0991cb862ac142031d4b <9240fc1f2cde5331c61608da21b00394602ca762"}, {"id": "1f932eab-2ff4-35ed-8879-328f482ad4c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b161eacd7fa4a2d765724b5504ac6cc388e48f80 <7a1781a2f3a9667b3065d402d1f11986a2363e08"}, {"id": "2237e466-b258-3eb9-8ec0-8a3ccb7434fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "bbc310caa2b6bf5fe42896ba27da0fbc12e4ac51 <be00deee60044ffa820f9436415caeb665b2cda0"}, {"id": "32f3563f-997a-3100-99ac-71120449f172", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "34865089-cf07-3ef0-a02b-fd1ad23f00c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "30d1d9f3495463f7c026e4c553127f79b486fcd6 <c25587fa26761e623198b4f47151fe79d09ccde6"}, {"id": "3ad18074-c3f0-39d6-94a5-3786b9470f9d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3c86ec1a-9d10-36f1-98da-72ee18db4a5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.111 <6.12.112"}, {"id": "65e10aaf-edd0-3b5d-b81f-1793deebc527", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b230e5bf501c5edaf2eb0991cb862ac142031d4b <6d91041bb38b97e2feb625123cc0529d7b83a0e1"}, {"id": "763646c4-77fd-3f57-8f84-3f37aef6666a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "82d985c9-f1c8-3b26-9381-1acbfbec25d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "a432ff80-63f2-3dec-8023-3559b1faafd3", "pro